// endpoint_close_workspace.proto — CloseWorkspace: the USER's close. SIDEBAR
// section. Closing is a VIEW act: the workspace leaves the tab-bar and its
// buffers close, but the daemon↔shim session is UNTOUCHED — keepalives and
// everything else continue; the workspace is merely unviewed. The host
// command is a thin wrapper: send, await the ack, then tear the tab down —
// every piece of real machinery is the daemon's.
//
// A close REQUIRES QUIET: no turn in flight, no live async work, and NO
// HELD PROMPTS — a held prompt is undelivered user intent, and a close may
// never silently discard it; the user releases or drops it in the tray
// first. A busy workspace refuses, and the refusal MANIFESTS IN THE FOOTER (status
// `closing`, sub-status `close blocked`, the daemon's composed reasons as
// the activity line) — pushed on the footer stream beside this response, so
// this response never restates the reasons. The user waits or interrupts
// the work the normal way, then closes again.

